WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.546
 Go, ha.

00:00:01.546 --> 00:00:02.070
And drop.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.780
Whatever you're curious
about, dive into it,

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:09.550
understand it, and
then rip it apart.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:13.300
When I was 10 years old, I
took my first hip-hop class.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.250
I naturally went
against the grain

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.937
and that ended up
being my magic.

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:20.799
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.750
For the first time ever,
I'll be sharing my secrets

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.640
and techniques to
my creative process.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.220
Let's go, girls, performance.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.500
You will learn the ins and
outs of how to discover

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.593
your true voice as a creative.

00:00:35.593 --> 00:00:37.010
There's so many
different ways you

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.560
can use movement to kind
of unfold the next group.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.770
I'm going to use
the curtain effect.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.260
The girls have gone
from covering the boys

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.110
into two straight lines on
the sides within eight counts.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.960
Just feels energetic,
it feels surprising,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.510
and it really makes a smooth
and seamless transition

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.070
for the next group.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:58.670
Let's break down the power
of eye contact to camera.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.770
I've told her that the
camera is a piece of meat

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:02.660
and she hasn't eaten in days.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.880
In her eyes, she's
telling the story.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.620
And as a viewer, we're now
mesmerized by her performance.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.810
Going drop and
chop, smooth, pop.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.610
I haven't always been confident.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.250
The truth is, it's been
such a long journey.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.438
Growing up, I always
felt like an outcast.

00:01:18.438 --> 00:01:20.480
You know, I didn't look
like a commercial dancer,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.780
so I kind of took that and
turned it into my superpower.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.180
It's about looking at
yourself and thinking,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.890
"What makes me unique?"

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.580
And once you can discover that,
appreciate it, and put it out

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.475
into the world, then you're
really using your voice.

00:01:36.475 --> 00:01:38.100
I really believe
that's what it's about

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.230
is understanding what's
within, understanding

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.520
what you stand for.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.830
Understanding how you
want to change the world.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.350
Because that's what dance does.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:45.850
Good.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:46.410
Cool.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.390
It changes the world.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.520
You can change the world.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.190
I'm Parris Goebel, and
this is my MasterClass.

